                                                "text": "An heritable crown, or an heritable throne, or by what other fanciful name such things may be called, have no other significant explanation than that mankind are heritable property."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "27b80ebb-3c89-3a34-8300-252a3eed84ad",
                                        "entry_id": "60a885a4-adfe-346f-86e8-92946fbb1e9c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Genetically transmissible from parent to offspring; hereditary."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "654742f0-0f9d-4312-a501-6ddd7f845c2e",
                                                "sense_id": "27b80ebb-3c89-3a34-8300-252a3eed84ad",
                                                "text": "But if we consider that all heritable variations must have their roots in the germ-plasm, and further, that when personal selection does not intervene, ..."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c55273db-6908-4368-94b8-56b66cd2bb74",
                                                "sense_id": "27b80ebb-3c89-3a34-8300-252a3eed84ad",
                                                "text": "Whether they are involved in carcinogenesis by induction of a heritable lesion would depend, I believe, on their ability either to mispair or to misrepair."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a036f144-eb20-4b8c-8228-7fb79ee61f59",
                                                "sense_id": "27b80ebb-3c89-3a34-8300-252a3eed84ad",
                                                "text": "The colour of a person’s hair is one of the most heritable features of their appearance, with studies on twins suggesting that genetics explains up to 97% of hair colour."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0db94b93-c6f0-4adc-b918-2c6c512d47c1",
                        "source_entry_id": "0fd167f8-fb77-32f4-9359-82bfa3417d33",
                        "source_sense_id": "e2769476-646d-3a96-8509-2acee447f5e7",
                        "source_sense_description": "alle Bedingungen erfüllend, die notwendig sind, um zu erben",
                        "target_lang_word": "inheritable",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "inheritable",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "257279c8-e2f8-3eb8-9968-45cf1aad7b5e",
                                        "entry_id": "d485bfcd-5f5b-3b7a-90bc-291be46f9e88",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "That can be inherited."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "72f740f9-34c0-4532-a90c-1a7106aca9b5",
                                                "sense_id": "257279c8-e2f8-3eb8-9968-45cf1aad7b5e",
                                                "text": "an inheritable estate or title"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "adfdd5ed-d220-4d1f-9685-36c48c874b64",
                                                "sense_id": "257279c8-e2f8-3eb8-9968-45cf1aad7b5e",
                                                "text": "an inheritable disease"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "faa951c8-dc7b-36ef-8a5c-bdfe7baeb2e6",
                                        "entry_id": "d485bfcd-5f5b-3b7a-90bc-291be46f9e88",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Capable of taking by inheritance, or of receiving by descent; capable of succeeding to, as an heir."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b4606dcb-f108-45eb-a541-645eb66c5697",
                                                "sense_id": "faa951c8-dc7b-36ef-8a5c-bdfe7baeb2e6",
                                                "text": "By attainder […] the blood of the person attainted is so corrupted as to be rendered no longer inheritable."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "12dcc5af-026c-4dc5-8184-02ddd4113c26",
                                                "sense_id": "faa951c8-dc7b-36ef-8a5c-bdfe7baeb2e6",
                                                "text": "The eldest daughter of the king is also alone inheritable to the crown on failure of issue male."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
